  converted weights are in `licenses/`.
* **SMPL / SMPL-H.** Released by the Max Planck Institute under a non-commercial
  research license; the model file is never redistributed here.
* **Third-party binaries.** ONNX Runtime (MIT), PyTorch / LibTorch
  (BSD-3-Clause), ffmpeg (GPLv3 for the build shipped in a packaged install),
  CUDA / cuDNN (NVIDIA EULA), YOLOv8 (AGPL-3.0) keep their own terms; see
  `licenses/RUNTIME-BINARIES.md`.
* **Documentation and screenshots** under `docs/`, which are working notes and
  are not part of the released tree.

Attribution
-----------

VeloMocap is an independent re-implementation of the RGB MoCap pipeline
(https://github.com/toyxyz/toyxyz_RGBMocap, MIT licensed). No source code from
that project is included; the pipeline structure, model usage and export
formats were studied from it.

The body model maths (SMPL/SMPL-X linear blend skinning, shape and pose blend
shapes) follows the published formulations of Loper et al. 2015 and
Pavlakos et al. 2019.
